#Donor/acceptor classification for the dynamic hydrogen-bond mechanism.
#
#Format: <resname> <type> <donor> <acceptor> [<antecedent> [[~|^]<second>[:angle]]]
#
#ATOMS ARE NAMED BY THEIR GROUP, which is the first column of the .grp -- AN for
#alanine's backbone nitrogen, ACA for its alpha carbon. That is the name the
#topology carries once it has been reduced, so there is ONE convention and
#nothing to translate: no .grp to restate in the .msp, no second copy of this
#table in another spelling, and no guessing.
#
#The one exception is a CROSS-RESIDUE antecedent, '-C' or '+P', which cannot be
#a group name: the type of an atom in the neighbouring residue depends on which
#residue that is. Those are written as plain atom names, and pdb2spn records
#what its .grp renamed so that they resolve exactly -- see
#spn::Particle::getOriginalName.
#
#One file per kind of structure, deliberately: protein, DNA and RNA
#chemistries are read side by side and keeping them apart is what makes either
#one legible. Concatenate them when a system has both -- the type names cannot
#collide, since amber.grp prefixes protein types with an UPPERCASE residue
#letter and the nucleic ones use lowercase.
#
#The classification is not invented here: it follows HBPLUS (McDonald &
#Thornton) and Reduce/Probe, and the files it replaces carried it unchanged.

ACE  XO    0 2 XC

ALA  AN    1 0 ACA -C
ALA  AO    0 2 AC

ARG  RN    1 0 RCA -C
ARG  RO    0 2 RC
ARG  RNE   1 0 RCD
ARG  RNH1   2 0 RCZ   ~RNE
ARG  RNH2   2 0 RCZ   ~RNE

ASN  NN    1 0 NCA -C
ASN  NO    0 2 NC
ASN  NND2   2 0 NCG   ~NOD1
ASN  NOD1   0 2 NCG   ~NND2

ASP  DN    1 0 DCA -C
ASP  DO    0 2 DC
ASP  DOD1  0 2 DCG
ASP  DOD2  0 2 DCG

CYS  CN    1 0 CCA -C
CYS  CO    0 2 CC
CYS  CSG   1 1 CCB

GLN  QN    1 0 QCA -C
GLN  QO    0 2 QC
GLN  QNE2   2 0 QCD   ~QOE1
GLN  QOE1   0 2 QCD   ~QNE2

GLU  EN    1 0 ECA -C
GLU  EO    0 2 EC
GLU  EOE1  0 2 ECD
GLU  EOE2  0 2 ECD

GLY  GN    1 0 GCA -C
GLY  GO    0 2 GC

HIS  HN    1 0 HCA -C
HIS  HO    0 2 HC
HIS  HND1  1 1 HCE1
HIS  HNE2  1 1 HCE1

ILE  IN    1 0 ICA -C
ILE  IO    0 2 IC

LEU  LN    1 0 LCA -C
LEU  LO    0 2 LC

LYS  KN    1 0 KCA -C
LYS  KO    0 2 KC
LYS  KNZ   3 0 KCE

MET  MN    1 0 MCA -C
MET  MO    0 2 MC

NME  ZN    1 0 ZC

PHE  FN    1 0 FCA -C
PHE  FO    0 2 FC

PRO  PO    0 2 PC

SER  SN    1 0 SCA -C
SER  SO    0 2 SC
SER  SOG   1 2 SCB

THR  TN    1 0 TCA -C
THR  TO    0 2 TC
THR  TOG1  1 2 TCB

TRP  WN    1 0 WCA -C
TRP  WO    0 2 WC
TRP  WNE1  1 0 WCD1

TYR  YN    1 0 YCA -C
TYR  YO    0 2 YC
TYR  YOH   1 2 YCZ

VAL  VN    1 0 VCA -C
VAL  VO    0 2 VC
